{"name":"Royalty Loyalty","hex":"#ae58ab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"royalty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The rank, status, power or authority of a monarch.","People of royal rank, plus their families, treated as a group."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/royalty"},{"term":"loyalty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being loyal; fidelity.","Faithfulness or devotion to some person, cause or nation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loyalty"}],"entries":[{"title":"Loyalty","blocks":[{"text":"Loyalty is a devotion to a country, philosophy, group, or person. Philosophers disagree on what can be an object of loyalty as some argue that loyalty is strictly interpersonal and only another human being can be the object of loyalty. The definition of loyalty in law and political science is the fidelity of an individual to a nation, either one's nation of birth, or one's declared home nation by oath (naturalization)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Pledge_of_allegiance_to_the_flag%2C_8th_Division_LCCN2001703605.jpg/330px-Pledge_of_allegiance_to_the_flag%2C_8th_Division_LCCN2001703605.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loyalty","wikidata":"Q1132131"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Edwin_Landseer_Attachment.JPG/500px-Edwin_Landseer_Attachment.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Edwin_Landseer_Attachment.JPG/500px-Edwin_Landseer_Attachment.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Foxie, guarding the body of her master Charles Gough, in Attachment by Edwin Landseer, 1829","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEdwin_Landseer_Attachment.JPG"}],"sounds":{"royalty":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2a/En-us-royalty.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/2a/En-us-royalty.ogg/En-us-royalty.ogg.mp3"}],"loyalty":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/31/En-us-loyalty.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/31/En-us-loyalty.ogg/En-us-loyalty.ogg.mp3"}]}}}